# Git stores text files with LF line endings and checks them out with LF, as .editorconfig asks.
* text=auto eol=lf
# The golden fixtures are compared byte for byte with metadata Obsidian computed from them, so git must
# never change their line endings (CRLF note.md is CRLF on purpose).
fixtures/golden-vault/** -text
fixtures/golden-vault.metadata.json -text
fixtures/golden/** -text
# The screenshot baselines are compared too, the visible/*.txt snapshots byte for byte, see
# apps/obsidian-plugin/scripts/screenshots.mjs. Git still finds the PNGs binary by their content.
fixtures/screenshots/** -text
# The data.json shapes are read as Obsidian reads data.json, and the snapshots of what the plugin writes back and the
# settings tab shows are compared byte for byte, see apps/obsidian-plugin/tests/settings-fixtures.ts.
fixtures/settings/** -text
